# App Router Structure

This project uses Next.js App Router. Each directory under [src/app](mdc:src/app) represents a route:

- [src/app/actions](mdc:src/app/actions) - Server actions
- [src/app/api](mdc:src/app/api) - API routes
- [src/app/auth](mdc:src/app/auth) - Authentication related routes
- [src/app/dashboard](mdc:src/app/dashboard) - Dashboard pages
- [src/app/exercises](mdc:src/app/exercises) - Exercise management
- [src/app/workout](mdc:src/app/workout) - Workout pages
- [src/app/workouts](mdc:src/app/workouts) - Workouts listing

Route files follow Next.js App Router conventions:
- `page.tsx` - Main page component
- `layout.tsx` - Layout wrapper
- `loading.tsx` - Loading state
- `error.tsx` - Error handling
